    content: "When booking and verifying permits for Mount Ijen, strict identification rules apply at the Paltuding Ranger Station. Here is everything you need to prepare to ensure an effortless check-in.\n\n---\n\n## Document Requirements by Traveler Category\n\n### 1. International Visitors (Foreign Citizens)\n- **Primary Document**: Original Physical **Passport** with valid Indonesian immigration entry visa / visa-on-arrival / KITAS stamp.\n- **Name Matching**: The full name spelled on your BBKSDA entry ticket must strictly match your passport identity page.\n- **Photocopies vs Physical**: While high-resolution digital scans on your phone are accepted in emergency backup cases, BBKSDA rangers strongly prefer inspecting the **physical passport** during midnight check-in.\n\n### 2. Domestic Travelers (Warga Negara Indonesia)\n- **Primary Document**: Physical **e-KTP** (Kartu Tanda Penduduk) or digital IKD (Identitas Kependudukan Digital).\n- **Alternative IDs**: A valid **SIM** (Driver's License) or **Paspor Indonesia** is accepted if your KTP is unavailable.\n- **Children / Minors**: Indonesian children under 17 years old must present **KIA** (Kartu Identitas Anak) or an official **Kartu Keluarga (KK)** copy.\n\n---\n\n## Common Pitfalls to Avoid\n\n- **Typo in Passport Number**: Double-check your passport number when booking online. A mismatch may require manual supervisor override at Paltuding.\n- **Expired Identification**: Ensure your passport has at least 6 months validity from your Indonesian entry date.\n- **Group Bookings**: If you are traveling as a family or group, keep all physical identity cards together in an easily accessible waterproof zip pouch for rapid verification at the gate."
