    id: "best-jacket-windbreaker-mount-ijen-summit",
    slug: "best-jacket-windbreaker-mount-ijen-summit",
    title: "Best Jacket & Windbreaker for Mount Ijen: Beating Freezing Summit Winds Below 10°C",
    category: "Guides",
    date: "November 10, 2026",
    readTime: "5 Min Read",
    excerpt: "Summit winds at Mount Ijen routinely drop temperatures into single digits. Discover the ideal windbreaker, hardshell, and down jacket specs for the midnight climb.",
    image: "/images/HeroSection.webp",
    isFeatured: false,
    author: "Ijen Expedition Team",
    content: "Many first-time visitors expect Indonesia to be hot and tropical everywhere. While Banyuwangi city is warm and humid, **Mount Ijen’s crater rim (2,386m) and peak (2,769m) are a completely different climate zone**. \n\nBetween midnight and 05:00 AM, ambient temperatures consistently hover around **5°C – 10°C (41°F – 50°F)**, and strong winds off the volcanic rim make it feel significantly colder.\n\n---\n\n## Ideal Jacket Specifications\n\nA suitable jacket for Mount Ijen should provide two primary functions: **windproofing** and **breathability**.\n\n1. **Outer Shell / Windbreaker**:\n   - Must be **100% windproof** (nylon or polyester ripstop with DWR coating or Gore-Tex).\n   - Wind chill on the crater rim rapidly penetrates knitwear and standard cotton hoodies.\n   - Look for an adjustable hood with a drawcord to protect your ears.\n\n2. **Mid-Layer Insulation (Packable Down or Fleece)**:\n   - A lightweight compressible down jacket (600–800 fill power) or a 200gsm polar fleece jacket.\n   - Traps body heat while remaining lightweight enough to stash in your daypack during the strenuous uphill climb.\n\n---\n\n## Why You Should Avoid Heavy Cotton Parkas\n\n- During the first 1.5 hours of steep hiking from Paltuding to Pos Bunder, your body generates intense heat.\n- Heavy cotton coats absorb sweat like a sponge and cannot dry in cold air. When you pause at the windy summit, wet cotton acts as a refrigerator against your skin, risking mild hypothermia.\n- **The Golden Rule**: Wear a light breathable layer while moving, and zip up your windbreaker and down layer the moment you stop."
