    id: "layering-system-thermal-clothing-mount-ijen",
    slug: "layering-system-thermal-clothing-mount-ijen",
    title: "Layering System for Mount Ijen Trekking: What to Wear for Cold Midnight Climbs",
    category: "Tips & Tricks",
    date: "November 10, 2026",
    readTime: "5 Min Read",
    excerpt: "Master the 3-layer mountaineering system for Mount Ijen: base layers, thermal mid-layers, and windproof shells to stay comfortable through temperature swings.",
    image: "/images/pkg-bluefire.png",
    isFeatured: false,
    author: "Certified Local Guides",
    content: "Mount Ijen presents an interesting thermal puzzle: you begin hiking uphill in the middle of the night, work up a heavy sweat on a 30-degree incline, and then stand motionless in freezing summit gales waiting for the sunrise.\n\nThe only way to remain comfortable across both extremes is the **3-Layer Mountaineering System**.\n\n---\n\n## The 3-Layer Breakdown\n\n### Layer 1: Base Layer (Moisture-Wicking)\n- **Purpose**: Moves sweat away from your skin to keep your core dry.\n- **Material**: Synthetic polyester (Coolmax, Dry-Fit) or Merino Wool.\n- **Avoid**: 100% cotton t-shirts. Cotton retains moisture and stays wet for hours.\n\n### Layer 2: Middle Layer (Thermal Insulation)\n- **Purpose**: Traps warm air generated by your body.\n- **Material**: Polar fleece sweater or a packable ultra-light down jacket.\n- **Fit**: Snug enough to hold heat, but roomy enough not to restrict arm movement.\n\n### Layer 3: Outer Layer (Wind & Weather Shield)\n- **Purpose**: Blocks biting volcanic wind and misty sulfur vapor.\n- **Material**: Windproof windbreaker or hardshell technical jacket with zippered ventilation under arms.\n\n---\n\n## How to Adjust Along the Trail\n\n- **02:00 AM (Start at Paltuding)**: Wear Layer 1 + Layer 3. You may feel chilly for the first 5 minutes, but your body warms up rapidly.\n- **02:45 AM (Pos Bunder Incline)**: Unzip your outer shell to release excess heat and prevent sweat buildup.\n- **03:45 AM (Crater Rim Arrival)**: Put on Layer 2 (Fleece/Down) immediately underneath Layer 3 before your sweat cools down. You will remain toasty warm throughout the Blue Fire viewing and golden sunrise."
