    author: "Certified Local Guides",
    content: "Hiking to Mount Ijen burns approximately **800 to 1,200 calories** during midnight hours when your body's metabolic clock naturally expects to be asleep. Packing compact, energy-dense trail food is essential to keep stamina high.\n\n---\n\n## Top 5 Recommended Trail Snacks\n\n1. **Bananas**: High in potassium and easily digestible carbohydrates; highly effective at warding off nocturnal calf and hamstring cramps.\n2. **Dark Chocolate / Energy Bars**: Dense in calories and healthy fats; releases sustained energy while providing a psychological comfort boost on cold ridgelines.\n3. **Dates (Kurma)**: Packed with natural glucose and fructose for an instantaneous energy kick within 5 minutes of consumption.\n4. **Honey Pouches (Madu Sachet)**: Single-serve liquid honey packets are easy to swallow even while wearing a face buff and provide immediate blood sugar restoration.\n5. **Salted Peanuts / Trail Mix**: Salt replenishes lost electrolytes, preventing muscular spasms and fatigue.\n\n---\n\n## Foods to Avoid Before Departure\n\n- Avoid heavy, deep-fried meals or spicy curries immediately before your midnight hotel pickup. Digesting heavy oils while hiking uphill frequently causes acid reflux and nausea."
