    content: "While serious medical incidents at Mount Ijen are rare, being prepared with personal medications ensures that minor inconveniences don't ruin your journey.\n\n---\n\n## Personal Medication Essentials\n\n1. **Asthma Inhalers (Crucial)**:\n   - If you have any medical history of mild asthma or bronchial sensitivity, carry your **prescribed bronchodilator inhaler (such as Ventolin/Salbutamol)** in an easily accessible front pocket.\n   - Cold air and trace sulfur fumes can trigger bronchospasm in susceptible individuals. Keep it warm inside an internal pocket so cold air does not chill the canister propellant.\n\n2. **Motion Sickness Medication (Antimo / Dimenhydrinate)**:\n   - The winding mountain ascent from Banyuwangi or Bondowoso to Paltuding involves 1.5 hours of continuous hairpin turns in the dark.\n   - Take motion sickness medication **30 to 45 minutes before vehicle pickup** for optimal efficacy.\n\n3. **Antacids / Gastric Relief (Obat Maag)**:\n   - Early morning exertion on an empty stomach often provokes excess stomach acid. Chewable antacids provide rapid relief.\n\n4. **Blister Tape / Hydrocolloid Band-Aids**:\n   - Apply blister prevention tape across your heels and big toes before putting on your hiking shoes if your footwear is new."
